// `shrink-0` and `truncate` on one element cancel each other out.
//
// `truncate` does nothing until an element is narrower than its content, and
// `flex-shrink: 0` is the rule that it never will be. The pair reads as "cut
// this if it runs long" and behaves as "let this push everything else out of
// the row". Use `min-w-0 shrink truncate`, with a `max-w-*` when it should not
// take its whole share to begin with.
//
// A regex over the class string, not a JSX pattern: Biome's GritQL does not
// match `className=$c`, and a bare `$class` matches every node. Anchored, so
// it matches the string literal and not the elements around it. Covers `"…"`
// and `` `…` ``; a class built by a helper call is out of reach.
language js

$class where {
  or {
    $class <: r"[\"`][^\"`]*shrink-0[^\"`]*truncate[^\"`]*[\"`]",
    $class <: r"[\"`][^\"`]*truncate[^\"`]*shrink-0[^\"`]*[\"`]"
  },
  register_diagnostic(span=$class, message="`shrink-0` with `truncate`: a flex child that cannot shrink is never narrower than its content, so `truncate` never engages and the element pushes its siblings out of the row instead. Use `min-w-0 shrink truncate`, with a `max-w-*` if it should not take the whole row.", severity="error")
}
